  declared  cvunion                \CvUnionA = 47.7; \CvUnionB = 90.5
            reason: union bandwidth of each search class.  The two classes do not cover the same frequencies, so a frequency with coarse but no fine coverage carries no drift-resolving limit; conclusion 2 quotes both side by side so the primary search is not read as the larger one
  declared  fracmax                \HoFracMax = 0.47; \RcFracMax = 1
            reason: the largest fraction of the discovery amplitude the repeat coverage still excludes, in the pre-registered hold-out search against the primary census.  Two populations, and the difference is the point: every hold-out crossing is excluded at 0.47 of its amplitude or less, while in the census the individual limits run all the way to 1.00, which is why the census median is reported as a median and never as a bound on the set
  declared  fracmed                \RcFracMed = 0.43; \RfiFracMed = 0.5
            reason: TWO DIFFERENT FRACTIONS OF TWO DIFFERENT THINGS, and only the word "frac" is shared.  RcFracMed is the median fraction of the DISCOVERY AMPLITUDE that the repeat coverage excludes, over the crossings that carry an exclusion.  RfiFracMed is the median fractional POSITION of a released peak inside its own spectral window, which is the fixed-intermediate-frequency test of the interference appendix and is 0.50 because the positions are uniform.  Neither is a bound and they are not the same quantity in any sense
